# b27 — what `| logfmt` extracts from a line holding a malformed token
# (issue #507).
#
# Reference of record: grafana/loki:3.7.4 (revision b318f282), the build the
# rest of this corpus pins, with CI's shared configuration. Captured by push
# and query, one stream per line, `[10m]` window, 2026-09-13 and 2026-09-14.
# The reference attaches a `detected_level` label of its own; it is dropped
# from the expected sets, as the live replay leg drops it from every file.
#
# THE RULE (docs/api.md §2). A token is `key`, `key=`, `key=value` or
# `key="quoted value"` in full, ending at a byte at or below a space or at
# the end of the line. Anything else contributes nothing: the lenient scan
# resumes at the next token and `--strict` stops there, keeping the pairs
# before it. A closing quote must be followed by a separator or the end of
# the line. After a malformed token the scan skips to the next byte at or
# below a space OUTSIDE a quoted value: a quote opens a quoted value when it
# follows `=` or when the token has already opened one, and `\` escapes the
# next byte inside it. Error positions are byte offsets + 1.
#
# The reference's decoder returns a quoted pair the moment its closing quote
# arrives and starts the next key at the very next byte
# (`pkg/logql/log/logfmt/decode.go:151-186 @ v3.7.4`), and after a
# malformed token it skips to the next byte at or below a space with no
# notion of quotes (`:140-149`). So it can read text inside a quoted value
# as pairs. Where the two differ, the row carries our answer, the
# reference's captured answer in the comment above it, and
# `divergence(logfmt-quoted-value-ends-its-token)`. A value holding U+FFFD
# is replaced with one space there (`pkg/logql/log/parser.go:419-421`) and
# kept here: `divergence(logfmt-replacement-character-value)`.
#
# Case ids follow the plan's tables on issue #507: f01–f12 and g01–g06 (a
# malformed token, and the lenient decoder resuming), x01, x02, x09, x22,
# u01–u03, v01, v02, v04, w01–w06 and m01–m18 (quoted values), and three of
# the 400 generated lines (L071, L276, L306). The suffix is the mode: `l`
# `| logfmt`, `s` `--strict`, `k` `--keep-empty`. The 800 generated
# line–mode pairs are in `logql_logfmt_token_scan_matrix.rs`.
#
# provenance: captured
# (file default; see logqltest/PROVENANCE.md §provenance markers.
#  A row may override it with its own `# provenance:` line.)

load
  {service_name="lf27-f01l"}
  0s  {"a":1} x=2

eval instant at 60s {service_name="lf27-f01l"} | logfmt
  {service_name="lf27-f01l", x="2"}  0s  {"a":1} x=2

clear

load
  {service_name="lf27-f01s"}
  0s  {"a":1} x=2

eval instant at 60s {service_name="lf27-f01s"} | logfmt --strict
  {__error__="LogfmtParserErr", __error_details__="logfmt syntax error at pos 2 : unexpected '\"'", service_name="lf27-f01s"}  0s  {"a":1} x=2

clear

